course: dictionary
lesson: 13061
title: Words for feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Feelings are what goes on inside you, like being happy, sad, angry, scared or excited. Another word for them is emotions. «Lucy felt excited when she opened her birthday present.» Excited is one of her feelings.
explain: Feelings can also be the part of you that gets hurt. «You hurt my feelings when you laughed at my drawing.» Here the speaker is not talking about a body part. They mean their inside self was upset by what was said.
explain: Feelings can also mean your opinion or attitude. «What are your feelings about the new park?» asks what you think of it. Look at the words around feelings to tell which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Feelings are the things you feel inside, like happy, sad, angry or scared.
fact: «Feelings» is the plural of «feeling», so it can mean more than one feeling.
fact: «Hurt someone's feelings» means to say or do something that makes them upset.
fact: «Mixed feelings» means being happy and sad at the same time.
fact: «No hard feelings» means I am not angry with you.
exercise: «Mia said, "You hurt my feelings."» What does feelings mean here? | Shoes that are too tight | *The part of you that can be upset by what people do | Facts about the weather | Songs you like to sing
exercise: «Sam had mixed feelings about moving house.» What does mixed feelings mean? | *Happy and sad at the same time | Hungry and tired | Sure that the move was a mistake | Angry with everyone
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as feelings? | carpets | castles | numbers | *emotions
test: «Ana asked, "What are your feelings about the plan?"» What does feelings mean here? | A sleepy yawn | *Opinions, what you think about it | A weather forecast | Things that are hurt badly
test: Which phrase means "I am not angry with you"? | Hurt feelings | *No hard feelings | Mixed feelings | Share your feelings
exam: «In the story, Max's feelings tell the reader he is scared.» Why do feelings matter in stories? | Because they are always about the weather | Because they tell the reader the page number | Because they show the price of the book | *Because they show the reader what is going on inside a character
